<title>HUNGARY: Hungary household savings rise HUF 62.9bln in July.</title>
<headline>Hungary household savings rise HUF 62.9bln in July.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's net household savings rose 62.9 billion forints in July according to preliminary figures, the National Bank of Hungary (NBH) said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;(This figure) indicates that after a temporary slowdown in the first quarter of the year, household savings returned to the earlier trend of high levels and continuous rise,&quot; the NBH said in a statement.</p>
<p>HUNGARY NET HOUSEHOLD SAVINGS</p>
<p>    (in billion forints)  July 1997   June 1997    July 1996</p>
<p>    Forint savings	   2,629.4     2,573.5	2,068.9</p>
<p>    Foreign currency	   492.6	 484.5	  463.2</p>
<p>    Total savings	    3,122.0     3,058.0	2,522.1</p>
<p>    Total loans		  337.3	 336.2	  351.9</p>
<p>    Net household savings  2,784.7     2,721.8	2,170.2</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures are not inflation-adjusted. Inflation ran at 18.1 percent in July.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
